---
/**
 * A whole BLOCK of copy in all three languages — T's twin for content too
 * long or too structured for a string table (the legal pages). Each
 * locale is a named slot; CSS shows the one html[data-lang] names, so the
 * page re-renders in place exactly as T does.
 */
---

<div class="tb" lang="en"><slot name="en" /></div>
<div class="tb" lang="es"><slot name="es" /></div>
<div class="tb" lang="zh"><slot name="zh" /></div>
